-- Week of Mon 21 to Sun 27 September 2026, cooking for one — but one who eats two plates.
-- Everything below is scaled x2 for that reason: a "serving" in a recipe is a normal plate,
-- and a meal here is two of them. 13 meals to cover, Monday dinner through Sunday.
-- Shopping Monday evening at Royal Oak.

= 2026-09-21

-- 8 servings = 4 meals: Monday night, Tuesday lunch, Tuesday night, Wednesday lunch.
-- The rice cooker one, because the shop does not get home until 9pm. Ten minutes of chopping,
-- everything in cold, press the button.
-- x2 is 1.2 kg of rice, which is 8 rice-cooker cups — fine in a 10-cup machine, too much for a
-- 5-cup one. If yours is small, cook it as written twice instead.
@./recipes/dinner/Japanese Chicken Rice Cooker{2}

= 2026-09-23

-- 24 servings = 12 meals: Wednesday dinner through Sunday is 9 of them, the other 3 frozen.
-- ~30 minutes hands-on (chopping) and 2 hours in the oven doing nothing.
-- x2 is about 10 litres, so it goes in two dishes side by side in the same oven, same times.
@./recipes/dinner/Big Batch Bolognese{2}
